# Task 164-001: Debt Closure — debt-156-011-fix Bookkeeping

## Context

`debt-156-011-fix` (CRITICAL, sprint-156) is an open debt entry titled
"Code physically verified despite missing .result". The DIRECTIVES (Sprint 164 wave plan)
explicitly states this debt was already **semantically resolved** in Sprint 163 T1
(Spurious NO_GO Reconciliation Helper canlı wire — extension of Sprint 145-015 work).
Task 164-001 is a Brain auto-added priority fix for bookkeeping only — close the entry
in memory.db so it reflects the live fix.

## Approach

Bookkeeping-only update (no source code changes). Update the SQLite debt entry to
`status: 'resolved'` with `resolvedInSprintId: 'sprint-163'` metadata, then regenerate
`.brain/exports/debt.md` via the existing export pipeline.

This is the canonical pattern used by `archive-debt.ts` (Memory V2 DB-first per ADR-036
governance). No new module is added — we use `MemoryStore.upsert()` directly via a
small in-line script run with `tsx`.

## Files to Modify

- `.brain/memory.db` — debt entry `debt-156-011-fix` `status` field flipped to `resolved`
  with `resolvedInSprintId` metadata pointing to sprint-163
- `.brain/exports/debt.md` — auto-regenerated via `deckent memory export` (Active table
  loses the row, Resolved table gains it)

No `.ts`/`.js` source changes. No test changes (test gate from Task 2 is independent).

## Expected Outcome

- `npx deckent recall "debt-156-011"` returns the entry with status=resolved
- `.brain/exports/debt.md` Active table is empty (or no longer has debt-156-011-fix)
- Resolved table contains the debt with sprint-163 as resolved sprint
- `tsc --noEmit` PASS (no source changes — should be unaffected)
- selfAssessment: DONE if bookkeeping update propagates correctly to exports

## Risk

- If memory.db schema differs from expectation → fallback to direct SQL UPDATE
- If `deckent memory export` script unavailable → manually regenerate via a small
  re-export call (uses same MemoryStore APIs)

## Out of Scope

- The actual reconciliation helper wire (Sprint 163 T1 already DONE)
- Vitest failure fix (Task 2, separate worker)
- ADR-045 contract write (Task 1, separate worker)
